{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Breakouts: The model consistently fails to capture upward momentum spikes (e.g., the surge from ~80 to ~88-91), predicting flat or slightly declining paths while sentiment is positive. Apply a significant upward bias adjustment when recent sentiment is >0.5 and price momentum is accelerating.",
    "Excessive Mean Reversion Lag: Forecasts exhibit a 'flatline' bias, anchoring to the recent mean (~78-79) and ignoring structural regime shifts. When true prices break the 80 threshold, the model lags by 5-10 days before adjusting, causing large cumulative errors. Reduce the mean-reversion weight in the model during high-volatility regimes.",
    "Overshoot Correction on Dips: After major price spikes (e.g., >88), the model underestimates the subsequent correction depth, predicting a slow decline while actual prices drop sharply or stabilize lower. Apply a steeper downward correction factor in the 10-20 day horizon following a >10% price spike.",
    "Sentiment-Price Decoupling: High sentiment scores (1.00) are not reflected in the forecast magnitude. The model treats positive sentiment as a minor drift rather than a catalyst. Increase the sensitivity coefficient for sentiment scores >0.67 to align forecasts with the observed volatility range.",
    "Horizon-Specific Drift: Errors are minimal in the first 3-5 days but explode in the 10-20 day window. The model assumes a linear trend that does not exist. Implement a non-linear decay function for the forecast horizon that accounts for the observed cyclical nature of the price action."
  ]
}
